yosys: write_xaiger2 writes the holes outputs in port order

AigerWriter::write() numbers a module's inputs and counts its outputs in
port order, then collects the output literals by iterating the module's
wires, which is hash-dict order. For an ordinary module that only
permutes outputs the caller matches by name. For the holes module that
write_xaiger2 embeds in the .xaig (the 'a' extension: the logic of every
white box, one output per box output, in box order), the order is the
contract: ABC rebuilds box i from the outputs at box i's position.

With two or more white boxes, ABC's &verify -- on by default since yosys
#5620 -- rebuilds a box from another box's logic and reaches an input
the box does not have: Gia_ManDupCollapse_rec asserts Gia_ObjIsAnd
(exit 134) or, without asserts, segfaults (139). abc9_exe sees
output.aig already written and logs only a warning, so every abc_new
run with boxes -- every ORFS design with SWAP_ARITH_OPERATORS -- has
skipped its post-mapping equivalence check without saying so. The
mapped netlist is not affected: mock-alu's is byte-identical with and
without this patch.

test/yosys_abc_new_boxes reproduces it with two boxes of different
shapes.

Fixed on yosys main by 569e454cc ("Fix box models and output order"),
part of YosysHQ/yosys#6174, merged 2026-09-14, after v0.69; no release
carries it. This is that commit's output-order hunk alone. Not
upstreamed by bazel-orfs; carried in MODULE.bazel on yosys's
single_version_override. Retires at the bump onto a BCR yosys that
contains 569e454cc.

--- a/backends/aiger2/aiger.cc
+++ b/backends/aiger2/aiger.cc
@@ -814,13 +814,15 @@
 
 		// now the guts
 		std::vector<std::pair<SigBit, int>> outputs;
-		for (auto w : top->wires())
+		for (auto id : top->ports) {
+			Wire *w = top->wire(id);
 			if (w->port_output) {
 				for (auto bit : SigSpec(w))
 					// Each call to eval_po eventually reaches emit_gate and
 					// encode which writes to f.
 					outputs.push_back({bit, eval_po(bit)});
 			}
+		}
 
 		auto data_end = f->tellp();
 
